{
  "title": "People, pronouns and to be",
  "note": "Latin often drops subject pronouns because the verb ending shows who: sum, I am; sumus, we are. Learn the present of esse by heart: sum, es, est, sumus, estis, sunt. Latin has no word for a or the: puella is a girl or the girl. The verb usually comes last.",
  "src": {
    "t": "Allen and Greenough, sum",
    "u": "https://dcc.dickinson.edu/grammar/latin/sum"
  },
